OL,3,GNEWSAPlans to light up Belfast City
OL,4,AHall for Safe Abortion Day to not go
OL,5,Aahead, BBC understands
OL,6,
OL,7,FPlans to light up Belfast City Hall to
OL,8,Fmark Safe Abortion Day will not go
OL,9,Fahead on Monday after the Democratic
OL,10,FUnionist Party (DUP) used a council
OL,11,Fprocedure to challenge the decision.
OL,13,FThe landmark was due to be lit up
OL,14,Fgreen, after a request by the National
OL,15,FWomen's Council of Ireland and a motion
OL,16,Fbrought to the council by the Alliance
OL,17,FParty.
OL,19,FThat motion was opposed by unionist
OL,20,Fparties and anti-abortion
OL,21,Forganisations.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,417,410,260,120,0,100
